Package: rsemverse
Type: Package
Title: From RSEM Results to Analysis-Ready Gene Tables
Version: 0.8.0
Authors@R: person("Daiki", "Kumakura", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "55353329+DaikiKumakura@users.noreply.github.com")
Description: Turns RSEM '*.genes.results' and '*.isoforms.results' files
    into analysis-ready gene tables for human and mouse bulk RNA-seq. The
    files, listed in a sample table or found in a folder, are read into one
    table of expected counts, TPM or effective lengths with one row per gene
    symbol and one column per sample, using the Bioconductor annotation
    packages 'org.Hs.eg.db' and 'org.Mm.eg.db'. The same table is then
    filtered (the 'edgeR' filterByExpr rule, detection thresholds with a
    count of genes kept per threshold, most variable genes), reduced to gene
    groups (protein-coding, mitochondrial, ribosomal protein, hemoglobin,
    sex-chromosome, spike-in, and rRNA, snoRNA, lncRNA and other types from
    a GTF file, with their share per sample and the read assignment
    statistics of the RSEM '.cnt' files), and summarized per sample (principal
    components, sample correlation, detected genes), normalized between samples (CPM, TMM, TMMwsp, upper
    quartile, DESeq2 median of ratios, quantile), transformed (log2, z-score,
    ranks, z-scores against a fixed reference group), and returned as a long
    table with the sample information or written with gene IDs and types.
    Transcripts can be selected by expression and effective lengths
    summarized. Filtering and normalization give the same results as 'edgeR',
    'DESeq2' and 'limma' without depending on them.
